  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "123ae5dfcd70",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "anchor": "tutorial-get-started-with-go",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Tutorial: Get started with Go"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "af635e43360d",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "In this tutorial, you'll get a brief introduction to Go programming. Along the way, you will:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c4cd2380352f",
      "kind": "list",
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "d6bcc5a8ea8e",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Install Go (if you haven't already)."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "459587d12fdc",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Write some simple \"Hello, world\" code."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "dc32329a2f75",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Use the "
                },
                {
                  "text": "go",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " command to run your code."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "cb7afa0d0f0b",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Use the Go package discovery tool to find packages you can use in your own code."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "12435c6ffc0a",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Call functions of an external module."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "de3498cfb490",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "anchor": "prerequisites",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Prerequisites"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "a4f92a579bf4",
      "kind": "list",
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "1acfbfb31aa2",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Some programming experience.",
                  "marks": [
                    "bold"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " The code here is pretty simple, but it helps to know something about functions."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "7aeee9ef2f8b",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "A tool to edit your code.",
                  "marks": [
                    "bold"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " Any text editor you have will work fine. Most text editors have good support for Go. The most popular are VSCode (free), GoLand (paid), and Vim (free)."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "900a9732f122",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "A command terminal.",
                  "marks": [
                    "bold"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " Go works well using any terminal on Linux and Mac, and on PowerShell or cmd in Windows."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "55aef9434ae3",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "anchor": "install",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Install Go"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "e82d52efa440",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Just use the "
        },
        {
          "text": "Download and install",
          "link": {
            "href": "https://go.dev/doc/install",
            "kind": "same_domain"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " steps."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8be6e34555c4",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "anchor": "code",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Write some code"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "e859967ee6f9",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Get started with Hello, World."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6d5f4959d1e3",
      "kind": "list",
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "0d7fff22e298",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Open a command prompt and cd to your home directory."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "1ba1b8015fbd",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "On Linux or Mac:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "f7115026ed95",
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "cd\n"
            },
            {
              "id": "5e9b9a17b587",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "On Windows:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "098747852bc5",
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "cd %HOMEPATH%\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "cbfcba89c3d5",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Create a hello directory for your first Go source code."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "5a2e0d957ce6",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "For example, use the following commands:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "2c82488da79b",
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "mkdir hello\ncd hello\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "22d77d6eff9e",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Enable dependency tracking for your code."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "96c880741b6d",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "When your code imports packages contained in other modules, you manage those dependencies through your code's own module. That module is defined by a go.mod file that tracks the modules that provide those packages. That go.mod file stays with your code, including in your source code repository."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "0c55e31fd4a0",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "To enable dependency tracking for your code by creating a go.mod file, run the "
                },
                {
                  "text": "go mod init",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ],
                  "link": {
                    "href": "https://go.dev/ref/mod#go-mod-init",
                    "kind": "same_domain"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": " command, giving it the name of the module your code will be in. The name is the module's module path."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "b4e15262434b",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "In actual development, the module path will typically be the repository location where your source code will be kept. For example, the module path might be "
                },
                {
                  "text": "github.com/mymodule",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ". If you plan to publish your module for others to use, the module path "
                },
                {
                  "text": "must",
                  "marks": [
                    "italic"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " be a location from which Go tools can download your module. For more about naming a module with a module path, see "
                },
                {
                  "text": "Managing dependencies",
                  "link": {
                    "href": "https://go.dev/doc/modules/managing-dependencies#naming_module",
                    "kind": "same_domain"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "7a5ce38a87fc",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "For the purposes of this tutorial, just use "
                },
                {
                  "text": "example/hello",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "96ccfc9642af",
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "$ go mod init example/hello\ngo: creating new go.mod: module example/hello\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "a509c243e371",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "In your text editor, create a file hello.go in which to write your code."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "0871965424f8",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Paste the following code into your hello.go file and save the file."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "cf83c7bedb61",
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nfunc main() {\n    fmt.Println(\"Hello, World!\")\n}\n"
            },
            {
              "id": "d88e23ae23c1",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "This is your Go code. In this code, you:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "423afd6bb19d",
              "kind": "list",
              "items": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "3eb184161611",
                      "kind": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "Declare a "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "main",
                          "marks": [
                            "code"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": " package (a package is a way to group functions, and it's made up of all the files in the same directory)."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "b860fb20aa43",
                      "kind": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "Import the popular "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "fmt",
                          "marks": [
                            "code"
                          ],
                          "link": {
                            "href": "https://pkg.go.dev/fmt/",
                            "kind": "external"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "text": " package",
                          "link": {
                            "href": "https://pkg.go.dev/fmt/",
                            "kind": "external"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "text": ", which contains functions for formatting text, including printing to the console. This package is one of the "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "standard library",
                          "link": {
                            "href": "https://pkg.go.dev/std",
                            "kind": "external"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "text": " packages you got when you installed Go."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "cace64d70c7e",
                      "kind": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "Implement a "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "main",
                          "marks": [
                            "code"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": " function to print a message to the console. A "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "main",
                          "marks": [
                            "code"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": " function executes by default when you run the "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "main",
                          "marks": [
                            "code"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": " package."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "93039ad241b8",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Run your code to see the greeting."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "22a884946b9a",
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "$ go run .\nHello, World!\n"
            },
            {
              "id": "871d63cc3792",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The "
                },
                {
                  "text": "go run",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ],
                  "link": {
                    "href": "https://go.dev/cmd/go/#hdr-Compile_and_run_Go_program",
                    "kind": "same_domain"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": " command is one of many "
                },
                {
                  "text": "go",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " commands you'll use to get things done with Go. Use the following command to get a list of the others:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "4cf2dc7122ae",
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "$ go help\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "84c46b4aae4e",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "anchor": "call",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Call code in an external package"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "78d59830409b",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "When you need your code to do something that might have been implemented by someone else, you can look for a package that has functions you can use in your code."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b1d7e5f26ace",
      "kind": "list",
      "ordered": true,
      "items": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "84b3a729f32b",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Make your printed message a little more interesting with a function from an external module."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "1d1b59a54dfe",
              "kind": "list",
              "ordered": true,
              "items": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "48984c8e9a62",
                      "kind": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "Visit pkg.go.dev and "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "search for a \"quote\" package",
                          "link": {
                            "href": "https://pkg.go.dev/search?q=quote",
                            "kind": "external"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "587526c23597",
                      "kind": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "In the search results, locate and click on the v1 of the "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "rsc.io/quote",
                          "marks": [
                            "code"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": " package (it should be listed with the \"Other major versions\" of "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "rsc.io/quote/v4",
                          "marks": [
                            "code"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": ")."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "d9a099153c7b",
                      "kind": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "In the "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Documentation",
                          "marks": [
                            "bold"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": " section, under "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Index",
                          "marks": [
                            "bold"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": ", note the list of functions you can call from your code. You'll use the "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "Go",
                          "marks": [
                            "code"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": " function."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "7735e857db36",
                      "kind": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "At the top of this page, note that package "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "quote",
                          "marks": [
                            "code"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": " is included in the "
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "rsc.io/quote",
                          "marks": [
                            "code"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": " module."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "c8ee4d9e0416",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "You can use the pkg.go.dev site to find published modules whose packages have functions you can use in your own code. Packages are published in modules -- like "
                },
                {
                  "text": "rsc.io/quote",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " -- where others can use them. Modules are improved with new versions over time, and you can upgrade your code to use the improved versions."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "f895b6e18e63",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "In your Go code, import the "
                },
                {
                  "text": "rsc.io/quote",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " package and add a call to its "
                },
                {
                  "text": "Go",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " function."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "27a88c9a8c88",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "After adding the highlighted lines, your code should include the following:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "7f4eaa86af50",
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "package main\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\nimport \"rsc.io/quote\"\n\nfunc main() {\n    fmt.Println(quote.Go())\n}\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "4e775dd69024",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Add new module requirements and sums."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "84880537d2c9",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Go will add the "
                },
                {
                  "text": "quote",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " module as a requirement, as well as a go.sum file for use in authenticating the module. For more, see "
                },
                {
                  "text": "Authenticating modules",
                  "link": {
                    "href": "https://go.dev/ref/mod#authenticating",
                    "kind": "same_domain"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": " in the Go Modules Reference."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "63e499823e0a",
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "$ go mod tidy\ngo: finding module for package rsc.io/quote\ngo: found rsc.io/quote in rsc.io/quote v1.5.2\n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "id": "9cd0b5514621",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Run your code to see the message generated by the function you're calling."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "48fbe8f62c97",
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "$ go run .\nDon't communicate by sharing memory, share memory by communicating.\n"
            },
            {
              "id": "38df1ffbb000",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Notice that your code calls the "
                },
                {
                  "text": "Go",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " function, printing a clever message about communication."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "8ad891041d31",
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "When you ran "
                },
                {
                  "text": "go mod tidy",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": ", it located and downloaded the "
                },
                {
                  "text": "rsc.io/quote",
                  "marks": [
                    "code"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " module that contains the package you imported. By default, it downloaded the latest version -- v1.5.2."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c485b2cead5e",
      "kind": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "anchor": "write-more",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Write more code"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4cdb90215c12",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "With this quick introduction, you got Go installed and learned some of the basics. To write some more code with another tutorial, take a look at "
        },
        {
          "text": "Create a Go module",
          "link": {
            "href": "https://go.dev/doc/tutorial/create-module.html",
            "kind": "same_domain"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
